  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [{
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: 'How do I verify a signed Traverse capability artifact?',
    acceptedAnswer: {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'A published capability carries two checks: a SHA-256 digest in contract.json (integrity — the bytes match what CI reviewed) and an Ed25519 signature.json sibling (authenticity — the registry signing key attested those bytes). CI rejects digest mismatches before merge; after merge, signing CI attaches signature.json for non-deprecated WASM-backed versions. Callers should pin by digest and verify the signature against the published public key — not trust a naked URL.',
